  "verses": {
    "verse": [
      [
        "'Tis the last rose of summer,",
        "left blooming alone;",
        "all her lovely companions",
        "are faded and gone.",
        "No flower of her kindred,",
        "no rosebud is nigh,",
        "to reflect back her blushes,",
        "or give sigh for sigh."
      ],
      [
        "I'll not leave thee, thou lone one,",
        "to pine on the stem;",
        "since the lovely are sleeping,",
        "go, sleep thou with them.",
        "Thus kindly I scatter",
        "thy leaves o'er the bed",
        "where thy mates of the garden",
        "lie scentless and dead."
      ],
      [
        "So soon may I follow,",
        "when friendships decay,",
        "and from love's shining circle",
        "the gems drop away!",
        "When true hearts lie withered,",
        "and fond ones are flown,",
        "oh! who would inhabit",
        "this bleak world alone?"
      ]
    ],
    "coda": [
      [
        "To reflect back her blushes,",
        "or give sigh for sigh."
      ],
      [
        "Where thy mates of the garden",
        "lie scentless and dead."
      ],
      [
        "Oh! who would inhabit",
        "this bleak world alone?"
      ]
    ]
  },
  "arrangerNotes": "Verse 1, vocal line, verified against the Mutopia LilyPond score; the repeat is written out with the second (final) ending, which repeats the last two lines, and the score's rests are kept. Grace notes are left out. Simplification: one chromatic A♯ (passing note in 'no rosebud') is played as 6 (A). Range 1 to high 1. C and D arrangements use identical degree sequences (both fit their drums). Lyrics of the added verses: Verses 2–3: Thomas Moore (1813), from the same Mutopia LilyPond score the melody was checked against, where they are set under the same notes (https://www.mutopiaproject.org/ftp/MooreT/lrose/lrose.ly); compare Poems That Every Child Should Know (1904) on Wikisource. As in verse 1, each verse ends by repeating its last two lines (the 'coda' section).",
  "verified": true
}
